1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,100
What if you could see
what your agent remembers?

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:07,000
Meet code-review-graph.

3
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:11,000
You ask: “Reply in British English,
and use em dashes.”

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The prompt is captured
before the agent starts work.

5
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:20,000
Two preferences become memory nodes.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,200
Only your prompts create memories.

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:26,000
The agent’s replies are never used
to invent them.

8
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:30,750
Then say: “Forget em dashes.
That was just for this task.”

9
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:34,000
The preference is forgotten,
while British English stays.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
You’re in control.

11
00:00:37,250 --> 00:00:43,500
The agent checks your memory,
then the existing code graph, then works.

12
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:45,000
Two separate stores.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
No permanent cross-graph edges.

14
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:50,250
Lovable shows your memory graph.

15
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:54,250
As you chat across tools,
new nodes join the same graph.

16
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:56,000
You can inspect and edit it.

17
00:00:56,150 --> 00:00:57,050
code-review-graph.

18
00:00:57,050 --> 00:01:00,000
Your memory.
Your control.
